          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:54b42bc3283d09139c0be686b610ea67af84bc369556ff673366945ef372bb32:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_27cd24e0eecf4c5694152584dce33e8c",
      "statement": "The compose file uses the host network by default because Wake-on-LAN is a UDP broadcast that never leaves Docker's bridge, and automatic TV discovery probes the container's own /24 over HTTP, which on the bridge is Docker's subnet rather than the LAN; on the bridge a ports mapping is used and TVs are added by address.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://backend/docker-compose.yml#L16-L18",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:4c0b09b94944a2704bbfc843f85666e8f7dd7cc5ca9d7bad3a3cf8456eb545f5:"
